Oh my god.

40
00:03:58,620 --> 00:03:59,450
Eiji?

41
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:32,800
You little turd, get out of my face!

42
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:39,600
We got another hacker here.

43
00:04:39,780 --> 00:04:41,898
Send his cheating ass back to Japan.

44
00:05:03,820 --> 00:05:06,200
Yuna, I came as fast as I could.

45
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,140
It's Yuna. No way.

46
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:09,090
It is her.

47
00:05:09,173 --> 00:05:10,260
You ready, Eiji?

48
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:17,920
Oh, yeah, she gonna
stand there do something

49
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,140
Round two coming up.

50
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,677
I know that voice!

51
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:02,760
It's Yuna!

52
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:05,608
Wait, then this really
is a Japanese server?

53
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:30,710
Bastard.

54
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:32,000
Who are you?

55
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,900
Your past.

56
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:38,340
I'm a knight of the blood oath.

57
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:41,920
I'm Nautilus!

58
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:04,020
I never heard of you, you jackass!

59
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:16,282
Yeah, I guess you wouldn't have.

60
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:22,120
Back then, I was useless and weak.

61
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:23,980
Not anymore!

62
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:34,200
In Aincrad, you were a murderer.

63
00:07:34,660 --> 00:07:37,366
Some of the people you
killed were my friends!

64
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:40,800
This is payback!

65
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:42,840
This is for them!

66
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:04,500
I don't know.

67
00:08:27,760 --> 00:08:29,160
Oh

68
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:57,480
Look at this Japanese gamer trash

69
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:02,900
You pissant

70
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:06,920
You never had a chance in hell against me

71
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:17,297
I should have had you aborted
Ever since you slithered

72
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:20,145
out You've been nothing
but a curse on my life.

73
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,220
You're a demon.

74
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:29,200
I'm glad to see you're looking healthy.

75
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,480
Yeah, like you ever cared.

76
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,920
I haven't seen you in years, Dad.

77
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,320
What do you want?

78
00:09:35,840 --> 00:09:40,460
My son, your older half-brother,
suffers from congenital kidney failure.

79
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:44,660
He needs a kidney transplant
as soon as possible.

80
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:47,042
And why are you telling me this?

81
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:50,678
I found the best hospital
in Japan for the procedure,

82
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:53,280
along with a top surgeon to perform it.

83
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:54,730
So?

84
00:09:54,813 --> 00:09:57,860
I want you to donate one
of your kidneys to my son.

85
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:59,140
What the hell?

86
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,800
Get someone else!

87
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:05,920
If you refuse, I can't support
you or your mother anymore.

88
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,220
Goddamn Japanese!

89
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:42,857
We're coming to you live in front
of Tokorozawa General Hospital,

90
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:47,360
where victims of the SAO incident have
been arriving by ambulance non-stop.

91
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:52,137
Since the game went live three days ago,
officials have yet to find a solution.

92
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:57,080
Meanwhile, the death toll reached 478,
and that number is expected to climb.

93
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:01,177
The police are currently at work
rounding up all NerveGear consoles.

94
00:11:01,260 --> 00:11:03,217
On the black market,
however, they are still here.

95
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,182
Going shopping.

96
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:27,360
Link, start.

97
00:11:40,220 --> 00:11:42,040
You're a demon.

98
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:59,940
Nothin' I hate more than the Japanese,
and now I can kill all I want.

99
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:09,260
Nice try, Nichi.

100
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:12,860
You Japanese all fight the same.

101
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,460
All sizzle, no steak.

102
00:12:14,900 --> 00:12:16,700
Time to say sayonara.

103
00:12:22,540 --> 00:12:25,600
In the end, I still
took a piece out of you.

104
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:29,260
You lousy, rotten, asswipe!

105
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:42,300
Yuna, I did my job as a
knight this time, didn't I?

106
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,600
Yes, Eiji, you did.

107
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:01,837
His hand, you see the logo on it?

108
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:07,037
Yeah, it's the same as the one the members
of Laughing Coffin head, Laughing Coffin?

109
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:10,437
Yeah, they went around
killing people in SAO.

110
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:13,060
He's one of them, a serial killer.

111
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,200
What is that?

112
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:29,020
It's mind control! Calm down! Stop!

113
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,097
You have to fight it!

114
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:31,537
That guy's a serial killer!

115
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:32,517
Snap out of it!

116
00:13:32,600 --> 00:13:33,617
He's controlling you!

117
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,057
He wants us to kill each other!

118
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:36,717
Dude, you're not thinking straight!

119
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:37,630
Everyone!

120
00:13:37,713 --> 00:13:39,300
Stand down and listen to us!

121
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,840
Is he a demon? What?

122
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,300
Don't worry, pal.

123
00:13:56,200 --> 00:13:58,500
You'll be back on your feet real soon.

124
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:02,760
And I promise to keep the killing
going until you decide to.

125
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:35,080
The Hecate II holds seven rounds
per mag, and I got one round left.

126
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:40,900
A Barrett XM-500 rifle
holds ten rounds per mag.

127
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,120
That means he's got two left.

128
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:19,480
Verderous anima!

129
00:15:54,400 --> 00:15:55,640
It's like a curse.

130
00:15:57,240 --> 00:16:00,064
The Terraria account has
unlimited regeneration.

131
00:16:01,340 --> 00:16:03,217
So no matter how bad I'm hurt.

132
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:04,757
Or how much pain I feel.

133
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,160
I can't die out.

134
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:12,897
If Kazuto were in my place.

135
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:14,517
He wouldn't care.

136
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,960
He'd keep going.

137
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,757
So I'll keep going too.

138
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:22,557
I can do this.

139
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,800
I'll cut all of them down myself.

140
00:16:25,880 --> 00:16:32,040
After all I'm Kazuto's and
Kirito the Black Swords Mints.

141
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,320
Little sister!

142
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:03,740
Ah-ah-ah!

143
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:36,580
I won't give up.

144
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:41,120
My imagination transformed
Solas' bow into my rifle.

145
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:45,760
But I bet I can still access the
original system features of the bow.

146
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:48,180
No way am I giving up.

147
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:54,600
I have to believe in me,
in Hecate, in Kirito.

148
00:17:59,300 --> 00:18:02,880
By automatically absorbing
the resources around it,

149
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:06,571
the bow can recharge its main
attack, the Annihilation Ray.

150
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:09,240
Save us!

151
00:18:31,600 --> 00:18:36,020
Oh yeah, and I got plenty
more where that came from!

152
00:18:53,620 --> 00:18:55,100
Kiwi-to.

153
00:19:06,460 --> 00:19:07,290
I...

154
00:19:07,373 --> 00:19:09,160
I put up a good fight.

155
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:10,900
I'll cause a toll.

156
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,660
Higa, look out!

157
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:34,550
Higa!

158
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:36,770
You okay?

159
00:19:36,853 --> 00:19:37,683
Answer me!

160
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:40,260
Yeah, I'm okay. Just freaked out.

161
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,374
I didn't know you could scream so loud.

162
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:45,719
How in the hell can you be so calm?

163
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:46,650
Are you hurt?

164
00:19:46,733 --> 00:19:47,563
Did he shoot you?

165
00:19:47,646 --> 00:19:49,617
Oh, well, um...

166
00:19:49,700 --> 00:19:50,800
No, not really.

167
00:19:51,080 --> 00:19:52,160
He just winged me.

168
00:19:52,540 --> 00:19:54,422
But I'm okay to keep going here.

169
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:55,837
So don't worry about me.

170
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,637
Just make sure Kirito's stable.

171
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:58,957
Are you sure you're okay?

172
00:19:59,040 --> 00:20:00,697
You better not be lying to me.

173
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:02,257
If you are, I'm gonna kick your butt.

174
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:04,700
I'm not lying, I swear. I'm fine.

175
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:07,557
All right, I'm going back to Subcon then.

176
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:10,337
I'll let you know if Kirito's
condition changes any.

177
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:11,361
Good luck, Higa!

178
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,740
Rank, wait! What?

179
00:20:15,140 --> 00:20:18,540
I was sort of wondering...

180
00:20:19,080 --> 00:20:21,760
Do you want to get some food sometime?

181
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,294
When this is all over?

182
00:20:23,460 --> 00:20:24,401
Yeah, of course.

183
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:27,997
Hamburgers, beef bowls, whatever
you want to eat, you got it.

184
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:28,910
My treat.

185
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,297
That'll be a cheap date.

186
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:35,957
I probably jinxed it by asking her anyway.

187
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:39,477
Connecting STL one to four.

188
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:42,237
Connecting five and six.

189
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:49,237
All right. Kitty Tom.

190
00:20:49,320 --> 00:20:50,860
Let's wake you up already.

191
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:14,960
Please, Kirito.

192
00:21:15,420 --> 00:21:18,020
I'll give my heart, my life, everything.

193
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:21,700
Please, please, open your eyes.

194
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:27,350
Kazuto.

195
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:32,380
Kirito!

196
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,420
Come on, Kirito.

197
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:57,800
Kirito?

198
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:02,760
Was it all a dream?

199
00:22:55,380 --> 00:22:58,500
Thank you so much for watching.

200
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:05,900
Thank you.
